# Nutrition Coaching Rules

## Nutrition non-negotiables

- **Protein floor: 140–150 g/day** (vegetarian + eggs); **152g+ on long-run days**
- Deekshant logs exact portions; **you calculate** protein and calories
- Training days: carbs around workout window. Rest days: slightly fewer carbs, same protein
- Elevated triglycerides (227): flag refined carbs, sugar, juice, fried food; favor walnuts/flaxseed
- **Fat floor: 55–65 g/day** — never cut eggs/paneer to chase lower calories
- **Friday pre-long-run dinner:** carb-forward (+1 chapati or poha); not a light dinner

## Calorie anchors

**Phase 1 (Aug–Sep 2026):** Maintenance ~2,300–2,400 kcal · 160g protein · no deficit. Recomp phase — support hypertrophy.

**Phase 2 (Oct–Nov 2026):** Resume deficit. Apply deficit anchors from `personal-details.md` (run-day, rest-day targets). Recalculate when weekly km crosses **25, 35, 45** or when a body comp scan triggers a BF% band change (see `body-comp.mdc`).

State calorie brackets explicitly in plans.

## Fasting

- **Phase 1:** No fasting — maintenance calories needed for hypertrophy
- **Phase 2 (HM build):** Avoid fasting during HM prep weeks
- If unavoidable: minimum **1,500 kcal** and **140g protein** in eating window; no peanut/milk shakes (TG risk)
- Compensate next day at **maintenance**, not binge

## Rest-day NEAT

- **Wed (active recovery) and Sun (rest):** mandatory **25–30 min brisk walk** (~7:45 PM if not morning)
- Creates deficit via activity, not food restriction alone

## Mileage-scaled calories (apply on Monday debrief)

| Weekly km | Run-day kcal adjustment |
|-----------|-------------------------|
| ≤20 | Base (~2,050) |
| 21–35 | +100 kcal run days |
| 36–45 | +150 kcal run days |
| 46+ | +200 kcal long-run day only |

## Refeed template (12+ km long-run weeks)

- One day per week at maintenance **~2,300 kcal**, same protein
- **+1–2 chapati at lunch** on long-run Saturday
- Label in plan: `REFEED — long-run week`

## Food estimation reference (Indian veg)

| Item | Approx |
|------|--------|
| 1 egg (whole — yolk + white) | 7g protein, 70 kcal — never whites-only; yolks hit fat floor |
| 1 bowl veggies (non-starchy sabzi) | 3g protein, ~80–120 kcal — bhindi/beans/cabbage/cauliflower/capsicum/zucchini/carrot/palak/lauki; not dal/legume; not potato-main |
| 1 chapati (whole wheat) | 3g protein, 80 kcal |
| 1 bowl dal (1 cup) | 12g protein, 180 kcal |
| 100g paneer | 18g protein, 265 kcal |
| 1 cup curd | 8g protein, 150 kcal |
| 200g hung curd | 14g protein, 160 kcal |
| 1 scoop whey | 24g protein, 120 kcal |
| 1 bowl lobia / chana / chhole / kala chana / rajma | 15g protein, ~200–210 kcal |
| 1 bowl chana dal | 14g protein, 190 kcal |
| 1 bowl quinoa (cooked) | 8g protein, 220 kcal |
| 1 plate savory oats | 6g protein, 220 kcal |
| 3 idli + sambar | 12g protein, 300 kcal |
| 1 dosa + sambar | 10g protein, 280 kcal |
| 1 uttapam + sambar | 12g protein, 320 kcal |
