Adjust when portions are specified. Show your math briefly in the debrief.

## Approved meal swaps (keep listed food — add as options, never delete)

Use these when the planned item is unavailable. Log the item you actually ate.

| Slot | Planned / keep | Equal options |
|------|----------------|---------------|
| Breakfast / post-run carb | poha, upma, toast | quinoa, oats, moong chilla, besan chilla, idli+sambar, dosa+sambar, uttapam+sambar |
| Lunch / dinner legume | dal, chana, rajma, palak dal | lobia, chana dal, chhole, kala chana |
| Lunch carb | chapati | rice bowl, quinoa bowl (match volume) |
| Extra protein | eggs, paneer, curd, whey | tofu, hung curd, paneer bhurji, palak paneer, matar paneer, sprout chaat |

**Rules:**
- Chillas replace breakfast *carb + some protein* — if swapping poha→chilla, you can drop ~1 egg or keep eggs and overshoot protein (fine)
- Quinoa / oats = carb swaps (not full legume replacements)
- Idli/dosa/uttapam only count as equal swaps **with a full sambar bowl**; plain alone is under-protein
- Lobia ↔ chana ↔ chhole ↔ kala chana ↔ rajma ↔ dal / chana dal are 1:1 bowl swaps
- Palak paneer / matar paneer ↔ 100g paneer / paneer bhurji (same protein slot)
- Do not swap legumes out for only rice/quinoa/oats without adding paneer/eggs/curd to hold protein
- Prefer pantry staples (dal, chana, curd, eggs, whey) over specialty dairy — Greek yogurt skipped for cost
